From 0bf5cbedd300fc21b8cd3f07dc6cc823227b4a8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 10:42:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/31] a210: vendor import: 45-boot-peripherals

Cherry-picked vendor enablement group 45 (45-boot-peripherals) onto Linux v6.6.141 as
the maintained A210 LTS branch (one commit per kernel/patches group). Applied
with git apply --recount; reconciled against vendor branch osl/a210-v2.9.0.
See kernel/patches/README.md and kernel/T2-DESIGN.md for group rationale.

Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>

v7.0 port adaptations (subsumed-by-upstream wherever possible):
- mmc/sdhci-of-dwcmshc: upstream now carries TH1520 support (th1520_init,
  sdhci_dwcmshc_th1520_pdata, th1520_* ops). The vendor a210 copy was a
  duplicate of that with an identical pdata, so zhihe,a210-dwcmshc now just
  reuses upstream\x27s th1520 pdata via one match entry instead of re-adding
  the ~650 duplicated lines.
- dma/dw-axi-dmac: upstream now has AXI_DMA_FLAG_USE_CFG2 + hdata->use_cfg2,
  which is exactly the CFG2 channel layout the vendor backported. Took
  upstream\x27s 16-channel-capable code and just added the xuantie,th1520 and
  zhihe,a210 match entries selecting USE_CFG2.
- gpio-dwapb: upstream already has gpiochip_generic_request/free and the
  set_config fallback the vendor added -- took upstream.
- i2c-designware: dropped the vendor i2c-DMA path (i2c-designware-master_dma.*
  and its Makefile hook) and the custom i2c_dw_dt_configure. Upstream heavily
  refactored this driver; the custom ss_hcnt/ss_lcnt props it read are not in
  the A210 DT, and i2c-DMA is a perf-only feature -- A210 i2c runs in PIO.
  Revisit if a peripheral needs DMA-rate i2c.
- 8250_dma: dropped the vendor "optional rx DMA" rewrite (used the pre-7.0
  xmit.buf API; only uart9 used 8250-DMA, non-critical) -- took upstream.
- 8250_dw: kept the vendor RX-timeout-workaround broadening, expressed with
  7.0\x27s rx_timeout bool: (!up->dma || !up->dma->rxchan) && rx_timeout.
- clocksource/timer-riscv: kept the vendor CONFIG_XUANTIE_SSTC CLINT S-mode
  timer path (config is in the A210 defconfig) alongside upstream\x27s new
  riscv_clock_event_stop().
- stmmac_platform: added snps,dwmac-5.40a to the gmac4 compat list (A210
  gmac fallback compatible).
- pinctrl-th1520, reset-th1520: took upstream (both now upstreamed).

These A210 DMA peripherals (i2c, uart9, generic AXI-DMA consumers) fall back
to PIO / non-DMA; flagged for hardware validation in kernel/T8 notes.

Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
